Nothing reads what is written here. The file exists so that
/usr/lib/steamos/steam-short-session-tracker leaves Steam alone.

The tracker counts every Game Mode session shorter than a minute as Steam
having failed to start, and after enough of them it moves ~/.steam aside and
unpacks the copy under /usr/lib over the top. On a machine where leaving Game
Mode is one button, a short visit is what a person does rather than a fault,
and the entry that follows the repair spends the best part of a minute
rebuilding Steam and then updating what it rebuilt.
